{{ instruction }}

Before you modify any repository file, investigate the task and write exactly one
JSON orientation packet to `/logs/artifacts/orientation.json`. It must be valid
JSON (not Markdown) with this shape:

```json
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "status": "complete",
  "pre_edit": true,
  "candidates": [
    {"path": "relative/source/path", "symbol": "optional.symbol", "reason": "short"}
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {"kind": "command|source|test", "detail": "short", "path": "optional/path"}
  ],
  "tooling": {
    "loomgraph": {
      "used": false,
      "commands": [],
      "workspace": null,
      "backend": null,
      "trust": null
    }
  }
}
```

Rules:

- `candidates` contains at most five production-code files or symbols. Do not
  list test or documentation files as candidates.
- Record only evidence actually observed. Do not include credentials, complete
  environment variables, or unbounded command output.
- If you use LoomGraph, set `tooling.loomgraph.used` to true and record the
  command, workspace/backend when known, and any trust signal you relied on
  (for example `resolved_ratio`, `partial`, or content-comparison status).
- Write the packet before any edit. Continue with the task normally afterwards.
